      "html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<!-- WCAG 1.4.8 | PASS | SYNTHETIC | Persona: Stefan (ADHD/dyslexia)\n     Text block meets all 1.4.8 requirements: ≤80 char width, left-aligned,\n     1.5 line-height, adjustable font/color. No justified text. -->\n<head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Blog Article</title>\n<style>\n  body { background: #ffffff; color: #1a1a1a; font-family: Georgia, serif; }\n  article { max-width: 66ch; margin: 0 auto; padding: 16px; }\n  p {\n    line-height: 1.6;\n    text-align: left;       /* NOT justified */\n    margin-bottom: 1.5em;\n  }\n  /* Colors and font can be overridden by user stylesheet */\n</style></head>\n<body>\n  <article>\n    <h1>Making Text Readable for Everyone</h1>\n    <p>Good typographic choices make a real difference for readers with dyslexia.\n       Short line lengths, generous spacing, and left-aligned text all reduce the\n       visual strain that comes from tracking long lines across a page.</p>\n    <p>Avoiding justified text is especially important. Justified text creates\n       irregular spaces between words that can cause \"rivers\" of white space,\n       making it harder for the eye to follow the reading line.</p>\n  </article>\n</body>\n</html>",
