      "html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<!-- WCAG 3.1.3 | PASS | SYNTHETIC | Personas: Stefan (ADHD/dyslexia), Ian (autism)\n     Technical terms are defined using <abbr> with title and linked glossary entries.\n     Stefan and Ian both benefit from inline word definitions. -->\n<head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Developer Guide</title></head>\n<body>\n  <main>\n    <h1>Getting Started with the API</h1>\n    <p>\n      This guide explains how to use our \n      <a href=\"/glossary#rest-api\"><abbr title=\"Representational State Transfer Application Programming Interface\">REST API</abbr></a>\n      to retrieve data from our service.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n      Each request requires an \n      <a href=\"/glossary#auth-token\"><abbr title=\"Authentication Token — a secret string that proves your identity\">auth token</abbr></a>\n      in the request header.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n      Responses are returned in \n      <a href=\"/glossary#json\"><abbr title=\"JavaScript Object Notation — a text format for storing structured data\">JSON</abbr></a> format.\n    </p>\n    <aside>\n      <h2>Glossary</h2>\n      <dl>\n        <dt id=\"rest-api-def\">REST API</dt>\n        <dd>A way for programs to communicate over the internet using standard web requests.</dd>\n        <dt id=\"auth-token-def\">Auth Token</dt>\n        <dd>A unique code that identifies you to the service, like a digital key card.</dd>\n      </dl>\n    </aside>\n  </main>\n</body>\n</html>",
